P(X = k) = \binom{5}{k} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^k \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{5-k} = \binom{5}{k} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^5
\] The probability that we have at least 3 girls is: \[
P(X \geq 3) = P(X = 3) + P(X = 4) + P(X = 5)
