\] \[
P(X = 5) = \binom{5}{5} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^5 = 1 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^5 = \frac{1}{32}
\] Adding these probabilities together, we get: \[
P(X \geq 3) = \frac{5}{16} + \frac{5}{32} + \frac{1}{32} = \frac{10}{32} + \frac{5}{32} + \frac{1}{32} = \frac{16}{32} = \frac{1}{2}
